# Aurora — SSO / OIDC & demo logins

How to sign in after install: email/password (default), or OIDC SSO
(Keycloak / Auth0 / Okta / Azure AD / …).

## Demo accounts

| Path | Username / email | Password | Notes |
|------|------------------|----------|-------|
| Email/password (default) | `marketing@zyvor.dev` | `Admin@321` | Seeded when `SEED_DEFAULT_ADMIN=true`. **Change immediately** outside a throwaway lab; set `SEED_DEFAULT_ADMIN=false` to disable. |
| Keycloak SSO (when you run a demo IdP) | `demo` | `demo` | Smoke-test only. Requires `SSO_ENABLED=true` and a Keycloak (or other) IdP wired via the `SSO_*` env vars below. |

## Email/password (default trial path)

No IdP required. After following `INSTALL.md`:

1. Open the web UI.
2. Sign in as `marketing@zyvor.dev` / `Admin@321`.
3. Change that password before any real use.

## Enable SSO (OIDC)

Aurora speaks generic OIDC discovery. On the API, set:

```bash
SSO_ENABLED=true
SSO_ISSUER=https://login.example.com/          # or http://<host>:8180/realms/aurora for Keycloak
SSO_CLIENT_ID=aurora
SSO_CLIENT_SECRET=<secret>
SSO_REDIRECT_URI=https://aurora.example.com/api/v1/auth/sso/callback
```

Register that exact redirect URI on your IdP. Restart the API after changing
env (compose recreate, or `kubectl -n aurora rollout restart deploy`).

**Compose / Helm:** put the vars in `.env` next to `docker-compose.trial.yml`,
or pass `--set env.SSO_ENABLED=true --set env.SSO_ISSUER=…` (and the other
`SSO_*` keys) on `helm install` / `helm upgrade`.

**Self-hosted Keycloak demo:** issuer is typically
`http://<host>:8180/realms/aurora`, client id `aurora`, demo user `demo`/`demo`.
The public trial package does **not** ship Keycloak images — bring your own
IdP, or run Keycloak separately and point `SSO_*` at it.

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| No SSO button | Set `SSO_ENABLED=true` and restart the API |
| Redirect / issuer errors | `SSO_REDIRECT_URI` and IdP redirect URI must match exactly; issuer URL must be browser-reachable |
| Need a login with no IdP | Use `marketing@zyvor.dev` / `Admin@321` |

